### 1. Register a new user with all required fields
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S123456",
  "email": "student1@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123",
  "fullName": "John Doe"
}

### 2. Login to get the JWT token
# (Save the token value from the response body)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student1@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 3. Test a public route (Should work without a token)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/faculties

### 4. Test a protected route WITHOUT a token (Should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/profile

### 5. Test a protected route WITH a token
# Replace YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE with the actual token you got from the login response
GET http://localhost:8080/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJzdHVkZW50MUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInVzZXJJZCI6MSwiaWF0IjoxNzkxOTAxNTM2LCJleHAiOjE3OTE5ODc5MzZ9.EXLgzC4S7eQOoFHDeBdbQNUA7aGBpf1tlTJgx7-F9yU